  "observations": {
    "whatHappened": "As h shrank, the secant through two points turned into the tangent at one point. Its slope at every x, plotted below, made a new curve: the derivative 3x² − 3, zero exactly where the original curve had its hump and dip.",
    "why": "The derivative is the limit of the secant slope (f(x + h) − f(x)) / h as h → 0. Where f has a maximum or minimum the tangent is flat, so f′(x) = 0.",
    "equationLatex": "f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h} \\qquad \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(x^3 - 3x\\right) = 3x^2 - 3",
    "realWorld": [
